WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.450
Two giant Asian cities.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:08.470
The UN's 2025 estimate for
Dhaka: almost 37 million people.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.650
Tokyo: 33 million.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.770
And Jakarta is bigger than
both, at nearly 42 million.

5
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.430
All three are megacities: more
than 10 million people each.

6
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.190
So why is Tokyo far more
tied into the global economy?

7
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.270
Is it richer?

8
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.210
Did someone miscount Dhaka?

9
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.410
More tourists?

10
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.310
In this mission, you'll find
out how cities are ranked,

11
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.410
and why size is not the whole story.

12
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.530
Then you'll map the links between cities,

13
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.870
and see how a loan arranged in one city
can fund a port on another continent.

14
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.770
Your mission: explain why Tokyo connects
to the global economy so much more than

15
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:46.990
bigger Dhaka.
